description:
Ship `pkix_chain::verify_code_signer` and a Basic RFC-baseline code-signing profile in `pkix-profiles`.

## Deliverable

### pkix-profiles: BasicCodeSigningProfile

```rust
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]
pub struct BasicCodeSigningProfile;

impl Profile for BasicCodeSigningProfile {
    fn id(&self) -> &'static str { "ietf.code-signing-basic" }
    fn version(&self) -> &'static str { "RFC 5280 + id-kp-codeSigning" }
    fn policy(&self, now_unix: u64) -> ValidationPolicy {
        let mut p = ValidationPolicy::new(now_unix);
        p.required_leaf_eku = Some(vec![ID_KP_CODE_SIGNING]);
        p
    }
    fn policy_oids(&self) -> &[der::asn1::ObjectIdentifier] { &[] }
}
```

Symmetric to BasicTlsProfile / BasicSmimeProfile already in pkix-profiles. Add OID constant `ID_KP_CODE_SIGNING = 1.3.6.1.5.5.7.3.3`. Add free-fn alias `basic_code_signing_policy(now_unix) -> ValidationPolicy`.

### pkix-chain: verify_code_signer

```rust
pub fn verify_code_signer<P, R>(
    chain: &[Certificate],
    anchors: &[TrustAnchor],
    profile: &P,
    now_unix: u64,
    revocation: &R,
) -> crate::Result<ValidatedPath>
where
    P: Profile,
    R: RevocationChecker,
{
    let policy = profile.policy(now_unix);
    verify_chain(chain, anchors, &policy, &DefaultVerifier, revocation)
}
```

No identity binding (code signing has no caller-supplied identity target). The wrapper is essentially `verify_chain` with the profile generic per PKIX-fmtv.7 (C2).

## Tests

- Positive: leaf with id-kp-codeSigning EKU + valid chain → Ok.
- Negative: leaf without code-signing EKU + valid chain → Error::Path (EKU mismatch via existing validate_path EKU enforcement).
- Generic-wiring smoke test with pkix_profiles_cabf::CodeSigningProfile.

